--- code
function getClaimThroughPrefixedSchemeApi(scheme: PostingScheme, ledgerKeys: PrefixedLedgerKeys): LedgerClaim {
  if (!ledgerKeys.canPost) {
    return LedgerClaim.Unknown;
  }

  return claimFromAnySupportedScheme(scheme, schemeId => Boolean(ledgerKeys.canPost?.(schemeId)));
}
--- facts

# claimed at this site by an earlier run:
A ledger host method such as `canPost` throws when its `this` binding is not the object that owns it.

contradicted: run10 `canPost` is static on both prefixed interfaces, so no `this` binding applies (the claim: A ledger host method such as `canPost` throws when its `this` binding is not the object that owns it)
